---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`About ${SITE.author}.`}>
	<h1 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg sm:text-3xl">About</h1>
	<div class="prose dark:prose-invert mt-6 max-w-none">
		<p>
			Hi, I'm David. Outside work I play guitar and trombone, sing in a choir, and like poking
			around with new tools just to see how they work and what they're actually good for.
		</p>
		<p>
			I'm an Azure Cloud Architect at glueckkanja AG, based in Bavaria, Germany. For the last
			several years I've worked on the unglamorous but essential part of the stack: building the
			data foundation — pulling scattered sources into a single lakehouse, structuring it, cleaning
			it up, and making it something teams can actually build on.
		</p>
		<p>
			These days that foundation is what makes real AI work — LLMs, agents, and automation that hold
			up outside a demo instead of hallucinating on messy inputs. This blog is where I write about
			that intersection: practical, customer-facing lessons from real Azure data &amp; AI
			engagements, not theory. (Colleagues call me Data Dave — now you know where the name comes
			from.) Opinions here are my own, not my employer's.
		</p>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
